<title>FRANCE: French CDR sells loan portfolio to GE Capital Corp.</title>
<headline>French CDR sells loan portfolio to GE Capital Corp.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's CDR, the state holding company in charge of selling off assets of Credit Lyonnais, said on Wednesday it had sold a property loan portfolio worth around one billion francs to General Electric Capital Corporation.</p>
<p>It said in a statement GECC had been won a tender organised by Bankers Trust.</p>
<p>It gave no further details of the sale.</p>
</text>
